Z||000005||Fformula88||09-15-2001||10:44 AM||||Try not to let those jerks get to you.<P>I had a guy at the oil change place (another customer) ask me how the alignment was on the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  I asked him fine, and why?  He said because he ehard it was impossible to keep Fiero's aligned properly!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  I told him I had never heard that (I hadn't) and that my father's 87 had been aligned once in 100,000 miles and still drove straight with even tire wear!  <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000006||JohnF||09-15-2001||08:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>Try not to let those jerks get to you.<P>I had a guy at the oil change place (another customer) ask me how the alignment was on the car  [IMG]<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I love it!  I'm over 120K and on my 2nd alignment (one every 50K)!  Perfect handling, perfect wear!<P>Thanks world!!!!!!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||JayUSA77||09-15-2001||09:43 PM||||i have a buddy with a new 2000 SS camaro and all he can do is make fun of my car, but i figured out why. Im putting my v-8 in with nitrous soon and he knows that my car will do circles around him and he paid 25000 more for it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> i dont care what people say i would rather make my car to what i want it to be and have it be unique rather than having any fool with money be able to buy it from any dealer in the world. my 2 cents.<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||09-16-2001||12:37 AM||||I don't hear any negative comments when I'm driving the quad around  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  mostly people staring and whatnot.  And if they seem like they know what they're talking about I pop the decklid and then they really get interested  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Come to think of it, even when I was driving around my 84 and 86 I didn't hear too many bad things.. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Joe Torma||09-16-2001||01:18 AM||||My trip to Car Parts last week...<P>Me: I need a MAT sensor for an '86 Pontiac Fiero.<BR>Dopey Parts Guy 1: *brings out book looks for 10 minutes* A MAP sensor?<BR>Me: No, a Maninfold/Intake Air Temp sensor.<BR>Dopey Parts Guy 1: *looks some more*<BR>Dopey Parts Guy 2: What do you need?<BR>Dopey Parts Guy 1: For a Fiero...<BR>Dopey Parts Guy 2: Ya know, those cars are...<BR>Dopey Parts Guy 1: Odd.<BR>Me: *annoyed and rolling my eyes* It's really not that different than other GM cars...just FWD in the back.<BR>Dopey Parts Guy 2: The story goes that they used spare parts to make that car.<BR>Me: *now looking upsidedown at the book for the part myself*<BR>Dopey Parts Guy 1:What do you need again?<P>Morons.<P>On the other hand, I had some people say that Fieros were cool and they really fly witht the 6cyl.  When my car was on the road many people used to come up to me and say usually don't like Fieros but mine was very cool.<P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/amsig.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
